# Conventional ignore list.
#
# Before 1.0, this repo *was* the user's ~/.claude — an in-place overlay on a live
# Claude Code install — so .gitignore had to "ignore everything, then allow-list"
# the framework files to avoid committing the install's runtime state. In 1.0 the
# repo is a normal application at $XDG_DATA_HOME/agent-ways that *projects into*
# ~/.claude (ADR-142); it no longer sits inside a CC install, so the deny-all
# posture is obsolete. Track by default; ignore only build output and runtime junk.

# --- Rust build artifacts ---
target/

# --- C/C++ (llama.cpp) cmake build trees ---
# llama.cpp itself is a git submodule (tools/way-embed/llama.cpp) — managed by the
# submodule, not ignored here. Only our out-of-submodule build tree is ignored.
tools/way-embed/build/

# --- Built binaries (produced by `make setup` / fetched from GitHub Releases) ---
/bin/

# --- Generated embedding corpus (built by `make setup`; may hold per-user vectors) ---
ways-corpus*.jsonl

# --- Python bytecode ---
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# --- Knowledge-graph metadata (Logseq / Obsidian) ---
hooks/ways/logseq/
hooks/ways/.obsidian/

# --- Local Claude Code runtime state in this checkout ---
# When you work on agent-ways with Claude Code, <checkout>/.claude/ accumulates
# session/marker/cache state — ignore it. But DO track the project-scoped dev
# harness: agent-ways dogfoods its own project scope (ADR-143), so its own ways
# and skills live in .claude/ways/ and .claude/skills/ and are shared.
/.claude/*
!/.claude/ways/
!/.claude/skills/
# ...except the way-authoring scaffold `ways init` regenerates on demand — it's
# generated (from TEMPLATE_CONTENT in cmd/init.rs), not a tracked source.
/.claude/ways/_template.md

# --- Secrets / local env ---
# The conventional (track-by-default) posture has no implicit safety net, so guard
# the common secret/credential shapes explicitly — a stray one is otherwise a single
# `git add -A` from being committed.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
!.env.sample
*.pem
*.key
id_rsa
id_ed25519
secrets.json
secrets.yaml
secrets.yml
credentials.json

# --- Logs, coverage, language caches ---
*.log
node_modules/
.venv/
venv/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/

# --- Patch / merge cruft ---
*.orig
*.rej

# --- OS / editor cruft ---
.DS_Store
*.swp
*~
.idea/
.vscode/
